==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|de|Centromer}}, corresponding to {{affix|en|centro-|-mere}} (from {{der|en|grc|μέρος||part}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛntɹə(ʊ)mɪə/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛntɹəˌmiɚ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|genetics}} The central region of a [[eukaryotic]] [[chromosome]] where the [[kinetochore]] is assembled.
#* '''1999''', {{w|Matt Ridley}}, ''Genome'', Harper Perennial 2000, p. 16:
#*: Every chromosome has a long arm and a short arm separated by a pinch point known as a '''centromere'''.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|centromerelike}}
* [[holocentromere]]

